cubic (2020.05) focal; urgency=low

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-20:

  * Optimized the progressor module.

  * Improved error handling on the Extract page and the Generate page.

  * Fixed an issue where the application would continue running in the
    background after exiting or would freeze when trying to exit after
    an error.

  * Improved application responsiveness during error scenarios and
    during page interruptions (i.e., when clicking the Back button or
    the window exit buttons).

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-19:

  * Fixed an innocuous "End Of File (EOF)" error presented immediately
    after the "Compress the customized Linux file system" step succeeds.

  * Fixed Bug #1879208, Update the customized Linux file system size
    fails with an error.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-18:

  * Fixed Bug #1879190, Cubic sometimes generates an ISO that does not
    boot.
  - Added a new progressor module to replace the current progress
    module. The new module uses a more elegant algorithm to accurately
    report a process' progress up to 100% and ensures process are
    complete before they are closed.
  - Updated the Extract page to use the new progressor module.
  - Updated the Generate page to use the new progressor module.

  * Fixed Bug #1879191, In Ubuntu 19.10, Vte crashes with a Segmentation
    fault when the user exits the terminal. (See similar Bug #1877232
    for Ubuntu 20.04).

  * Excluded the following directories from the generated ISO:
    - \proc
    - \tmp
    Previously, all files inside \tmp were excluded, but it is simpler
    to simply not include the entire directory, since it is recreated.

  * Updated the extract-root command to only extract the Linux file
    system if the existing custom-root folder has been successfully
    deleted.

  * Updated the terminate-process command to use negative pids so all
    all child processes are killed.

  * Added non-bold colored terminal font codes.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-17:

  * Fixed Bug #1877897, Copying vmlinuz fails on the Generate page when
    kernel files (vmlinuz and initrd) from the customized Linux file
    system have been selected instead of the kernel files from the
    original ISO.

  * Discontinued redundantly saving  preseed and boot configuration
    files files upon leaving the Options page, because these files are
    saved when entering the Generate page.

  * Because preseed and boot configuration files are saved when entering
    the Generate page, discontinued redundantly saving these files upon
    leaving the Options page.

  * Organized the constants and displayer modules.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-16:

  * Fixed an issue where the all three actions (locate, extract, copy)
    on the Extract page were always preformed, even if some of the
    actions were previously successful. This has the effect of
    overwriting the user's customizations.

  * Added project create date and project modify date to the cubic.conf
    configuration file.

  * Organized imports and performed code clean-up.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-15:

  * Improved logic to print the "You have exited the virtual environment"
    message in the terminal based on signal status.

  * Fixed an issue where the original ISO was not unmounted when exiting
    the application from various pages or when the next page is
    undefined.

  * Fixed drag-and-drop not working on the Terminal page to copy text or
    files.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-14:

  * Fixed Bug #1877232, In Ubuntu 20.04, Vte crashes with a Segmentation
    fault when the user exits the terminal.

  * Fixed issue where the message, "You have exited the virtual
    environment," is not consistently printed in the terminal.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-12:

  * Fixed Bug #1877193, The customized ISO always boots to the
    gnome-initial-setup instead of the desktop.

  * Added support for symlinks for the project directory and for the
    original ISO image file.

  * Improved the layout of the Generate page.

  * Print log output for all progress bars in increments of 10%.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.05-10:

  * Fixed Bug #1831859, Cubuc freeze after project directory selection
    due to exception:
  - If the original ISO is not available, but the necessary files have
    already been copied to the custom disk, then Cubic will present a
    warning on the Project page, yet will allow the user to continue.
  - On the Prepare page, Cubic will attempt to locate the kernel files
    on the original ISO (if available) and from the customized file
    system.
  - If valid kernel files (vmlinuz and initrd) can not be found after
    searching these two locations, Cubic will present an error to the
    user, asking the user to either install missing Linux image kernel
    files on the Terminal page, or supply the original ISO image on the
    Project page. In this case, Cubic will not allow the user to proceed
    until the issue is corrected.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-9:

  * Fixed Bug #1855153. Cubic will prevent the user from proceeding past
    the Project page if the custom ISO directory is invalid.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-8:

  * Fixed Bug #1876190, Cubic crashes with Failed to open file
    "pages/source_view.ui" error. Added pages/source_view.ui file.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-7:

  * Updated dependencies and versions. Fixes Bug #1876127.
  - Added python3-pydbus and systemd-container.

  * Set the style for the source views on the Preseed and ISO Boot tabs:
  - The system mono spaced font from org.gnome.desktop.interface
  - The Tango style scheme for colored fonts
  - The ini language for context highlighting

  * Removed prepare_utilities module and moved functions to prepare_page.

  * Renamed modules:
  - directory_file_chooser => directory_chooser
  - filepath_file_chooser => iso_image_chooser
  - constructors => constructor
  - display => displayer
  - navigation => navigator
  - process_utilities => processor
  - terminal_utilities => console

  * Removed print statements.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-6:

  * Removed icon theme related functions from display.py.

  * Changed the original ISO mount point name from "original-iso" to
    "source-disk" consistent  with the naming convention used with the
    custom iso, "custom-disk".

  * Adjusted the window dimensions to fit on 1024x768 screens. The pages
    are 976 px wide to allow space for a 48 px wide vertical dock. Pages
    use an aspect ratio of 3:2 for better readability. As a result, page
    height is 650 px, leaving 118 px available for window's title bar
    and horizontal docks of varying heights.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-5:

  * Added missing exception type, ModuleNotFoundError, to navigation.py.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-4 and 2020.04-3:

  * Corrected two errors ("TypeError: Argument 0 does not allow None as
     a value") on the Prepare page.
  * Moved cubic icons to /usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/status.
    Removed /usr/share/icons/Adwaita/, since Cubic can access the icons
    from hicolor for both light and dark theme variants. This aligns
    with best practices, since it is not always guaranteed that the
    Adwaita will be installed.
  * On the Packages page, set both the package column and the version
    column to expand.

  * Issues fixed in version 2020.04-2 and 2020.04-1:

  * Updated Cubic to use standard symbolic icons, which are responsive
    to light and dark theme changes and automatically adapt to hybrid
    header bars.
  * Removed dark and light icons from the /usr/share/cubic directory.
  * Added symbolic status icons in the Adwaita theme for cubic ok, cubic
    error, cubic optional, cubic bullet, and cubic blank.
  * Stopped monitoring style changes and dynamically updating the icon
    search path for light and dark themes, since this is no longer
    necessary.
  * Removed the PayPal icon from the Donate button.
  * Set the NEW_CUBIC_VERSION to '2020.04', so all projects created with
    a Cubic release prior to April 2020 will be migrated.
  * Corrected the Terminal Control Escape Sequence, used to reset the
    cursor position, to not print corrupted characters in Ubuntu 18.04.
  * Corrected an issue in Ubuntu 18.04 where the header bar title
    overlapped the tabs on the Options page.

 -- PJ Singh <psingh.cubic@gmail.com>  Mon, 18 May 2020 00:44:21 -0400
